# Frontend standards

- **Design doc**: For UI that displays projects, artifacts, or the game runner, follow the flows and artifact types in [docs/multi-agent-game-builder-design.md](docs/multi-agent-game-builder-design.md). Project page shows status per phase and artifacts grouped by team; artifact viewer supports structured JSON and file references (e.g. images via URL or blob).
- **Next.js**: Use the App Router (`app/`). Prefer Server Components by default; use Client Components (`"use client"`) for interactivity (forms, polling). Use TypeScript with strict mode; interfaces/types for public shapes.
- **Routing**: Use route segments for project and play (e.g. `app/projects/[id]`, `app/play/[id]`) when those surfaces exist. Keep page components focused; extract shared UI into `components/`.
- **API**: Use a small typed client (e.g. under `lib/api`) for REST calls. Poll GET `/api/projects/:id` for status and artifacts until terminal state; do not block the UI on long-running generation.
- **Phaser runner**: Isolate the game in a dedicated route or iframe so React and Phaser do not conflict. Load the game bundle from the API (script + asset base URL) and bootstrap Phaser in that context.
- **Testing**: Vitest for unit tests; Playwright for E2E (e.g. submit prompt, wait for completion or mocked path, open project page, open play, assert canvas present). Use Tailwind for styling; keep accessibility in mind for artifact viewer and forms.
